     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>We only set a session cookie once you add an article to your reading list. It stores the list of saved articles and nothing else. If you never use the reading list, no session cookie is set.</p>
+    <p>Your privacy choice (whether you allowed or rejected analytics) is stored in your browser's local storage so we don't have to ask again. It is never sent to our servers.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Analytics (only with your consent)</strong></p>
+    <p>If you choose "Allow analytics", we load a third-party analytics script that records the label of the link or button you clicked and a timestamp. It does not record form input, and it never runs on the sign-in or sign-up pages. We don't load the script if you reject analytics, haven't made a choice yet, or your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time via "Manage Privacy Preferences" in the footer.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Account registration and sign-in</strong></p>
+    <p>To create an account we only ask for a username and a password. We don't ask for your email address, real name, or any other personal details. These credentials are sent over an encrypted connection to our authentication service and are used only to create and secure your account.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Fonts and external requests</strong></p>
+    <p>Our fonts are hosted on our own servers, so loading a page doesn't send your IP address to a font provider. Our servers tell your browser to send only our domain name, not the full page address, when you follow links to other websites. They also disable browser features we don't use, such as camera, microphone, location, and interest-based advertising APIs.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
